 "description": "Gemini 4 Argon vs Claude Opus 5.5: 6 extreme zero-shot coding challenges, same prompt, one attempt.\n\nI tested Gemini 4 Argon (High) and Claude Opus 5.5 (High) head-to-head on 6 extreme graphics, physics, and audio DSP challenges: Verlet cloth tearing, GPU Navier-Stokes fluids, 3D soft-body XPBD with SDF raymarching, a 3D Voxel engine with Greedy Meshing, a polyphonic FM synthesizer in Web Audio API, and a Cyberpunk Pinball table with Continuous Collision Detection (CCD). Each model got a single zero-shot attempt in one self-contained index.html with zero external libraries or textures. Result: Argon won 4-2, completed all 6 challenges in 90 minutes vs 159 minutes for Opus 5.5, held a locked 120 FPS across all 6 challenges, and used 3.63M tokens ($6.26 USD) vs 13.01M tokens ($16.26 USD) for Opus.\n\nDEMOS AND CODE\nMixiuh Labs interactive benchmark: https://danpez.github.io/gemini-4-argon-vs-3.8-flash-benchmark/\nFull repository and source code: https://github.com/danpez/gemini-4-argon-vs-3.8-flash-benchmark\n\nCHAPTERS\n00:00 The token bill and the stopwatch\n00:31 Protocol and token audit\n01:15 Level 1: Tearable Cloth Physics\n02:26 Level 2: GPU Navier-Stokes Fluids\n03:33 Level 3: 3D Soft Bodies & SDF Raymarching\n04:37 Level 4: 3D Voxel Engine & Greedy Meshing\n05:47 Level 5: Polyphonic FM Synthesizer\n07:01 Level 6: Cyberpunk Pinball with CCD\n08:15 Results, times and token bill\n09:03 Lab Verdict\n\nTOOLS\n- Voice: Voicefy, my own cloned voice, running locally on my Mac (narrated in English).\n- Editing and captions: Reelfy + Mixiuh Labs Studio (custom pipeline).\n- Music: original chiptune generated by code + real captured Web Audio from every project.\n- Models: Gemini 4 Argon (High) and Claude Opus 5.5 (High).\n\nThe narration uses my own cloned voice with Voicefy (runs locally).\n\n#Gemini4Argon #ClaudeOpus #AICoding\n",
